tiko-lang is licensed IN PARTS. The part a file belongs to decides its licence.


1. THE COMPILER  --  GNU GPL, version 2 or later
------------------------------------------------

Everything in this repository that sections 2 to 4 do not name. That is the
compiler (src/), its tools and build scripts (tools/, build/), the package
library (pkg/: std, db, sys, tkl) and its own tests (tests/, except
tests/vendor/). It also covers the tiko / tiko.exe binaries built from them, and
the copies of pkg/ shipped under toolchains/.

    This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify
    it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by
    the Free Software Foundation; either version 2 of the License, or
    (at your option) any later version.

    This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,
    but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
    MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the
    GNU General Public License for more details.

Full text: COPYING.

tiko-lang is not a copy of fbc. It is a separate compiler, written from scratch,
and written in tiko: it compiles itself. From 2026-09-05 its developers have
been permitted to READ fbc's compiler sources, which are GPL-2.0-or-later.
Transliterating them is still not permitted; lib/rt/PROVENANCE.md records both
rules.


2. THE RUNTIME AND GRAPHICS LIBRARIES  --  GNU LGPL, version 2.1 or later,
   with a static-linking exception
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

lib/rt/   tiko-rt, a derivative work of libfb.        See lib/rt/LICENSE.
lib/gfx/  libtkogfx, a derivative work of gfxlib2.    See lib/gfx/LICENSE.

Each extends libfb's static-linking exception to itself. So a program compiled
by tiko and linked against either library can be distributed under terms of
its author's choice, exactly as a program linked against fbc's runtime can.

Full text: COPYING.LGPL-2.1.


